course: dictionary
lesson: 4669
title: Holder: a thing, a person, a champion
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A holder is something that holds or supports something, or a person who has or owns something. It comes from the verb hold. A pencil holder holds pencils, and a passport holder is a person who has a passport.
explain: «Close them in a busy market and you hear the stall-holders shouting.» The clues are busy market, shouting and hot doughnuts, so a stall-holder must be someone who runs a stall. Look for the small word inside the big one: stall-holder is stall plus holder.
explain: Holder can also mean a person or team that currently has a title or record. The record holder has the best result ever. When you meet a word you partly know, ask which meaning fits the sentence, then try that meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: A holder is a thing that holds something, or a person who has something.
fact: A «pencil holder» is a thing that holds pencils.
fact: A «ticket holder» is a person who has a ticket.
fact: A «record holder» is the person or team with the best result ever.
fact: A «stall-holder» is a person who runs a stall, as in a busy market.
exercise: «The stall-holders were shouting in the busy market.» What is a stall-holder? | A loud noise made by a crowd | *A person who runs a stall | A tall wooden table with a roof | A bag for carrying fruit
exercise: A cup holder is... | *A thing that holds a cup | A person who has won a cup | A team that is the champion | A ticket for a game
exercise: Sam is the record holder for the fastest run at school. What does record holder mean? | A runner who never wins | The person who writes the records down | A small box for keeping records | *The person with the best record
test: «The account holder paid the bill on Monday.» Who is the account holder? | The shop that sells the bill | *The person who owns the account | The child who counts the money | The bank that pays the bill
test: The title holder walked onto the field. What does title holder mean? | The person who hands out titles at school | A team that has lost | *The current champion | A sign on the field
exam: Which sentence uses holder to mean a person who has something official? | The pencil holder sat on my desk | The cup holder was empty | *The passport holder showed her passport at the gate | The holder was very tall
